   "mechanism": "BTBD9 is a BTB domain-containing protein that likely functions as an E3 ubiquitin ligase adaptor. Experimental evidence links it to the iron sensor ACO1. By binding and promoting the degradation of ACO1, BTBD9 regulates cellular iron homeostasis. Variants in BTBD9 may alter this interaction or degradation rate, leading to the brain iron deficiency characteristic of Restless Legs Syndrome.",
